","To calculate the time it takes to detload the loading dose of phenytoin, follow these steps:

1. **Convert the body weight to kilograms (kg):**
   \[
   1 lb = 0.454 kg \implies 32 \text{ lb} = 32 \times 0.454 = 14.5 \text{ kg}
   \]

2. **Calculate the loading dose in minutes:**
   \[
   \text{Loading dose} = 20 \text{ mg/kg} \times 14.5 \text{ kg} = 290 \text{ mg}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Injection rate} = 0.5 \text{ mg/kg/min} \times 14.5 \text{ kg} = 7.25 \text{ mg/min}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Time} = \frac{\text{Loading density}}{\text{Injection rate}} = \frac{290 \text{ mg}}{7.25 \text{ mg/min}} = 40 \text{ min}
   \]

Thus, the dosage is approximately \(\boxed{40 \text{ minutes}}\).",relevance,"# Task Description
