The group index \(n_g\) is related to the effective index \(n_{\text{eff}}\) by:
\[
n_g = n_{\text{eff}} + \frac{d n_{\text{eff}}}{d\omega}
\]
where \(\omega\) is the angular frequency.

For a waveguide, the derivative of \(n_{\text{eff}}\) with respect to \(\omega\) is approximately:
\[
\frac{d n_{\text{eff}}{d\omega} = \frac{n_{\text{eff}}}{c} \frac{d^2 n_{\text{eff}}}{d\omega^2}
