\[
\Delta E \cdot \Delta t \geq \hbar c /2
\]  
Given the lifetime of the σ⁺ meson is \(2.0 \times 10^{-22}\) s, we can solve for the uncertainty in energy:  
\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{\hbar c}{2 \Delta t}
\]  
Substituting the values:  
\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{(1.054 \times 10^{-34} \, \text{J·s) \times (3 \times 10^8 \, \text{m/s})}{2 \times 2.0 \times 10^{-22} \, \text{s}}
\]  
\[
\Delta E \geq 1.581 \times 10^{-13} \, \text{J}
\]  
