\[
k_f = A e^{-E_a /RT}
\]

where \( k_f \) is the forward rate constant, \( A \) is the pre-exponential factor, \( E_a \) is the activation energy, \( R \) is the gas constant, and \( T \) is the temperature.

Taking the natural logarithm of the Arrhenius equation:

\[
\ln k_f = \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT}
\]

From the given data, we have two pairs of \( k_f \) and \( 1/T \):

1. \( k_{f1} = 10^{-1} \, \text{s}^{-1} \) at \( 1/T_1 = 0.0018 \, \text{K}^{-1} \)
2. \( k_{f2} = 10^4 \, \text{mol}^{-1} \text{s}^{-1} \) at \( 1/T_2 = 0.0012 \, \text{K}^{-}^{-1} \)

Using the above equation, we can write:

\[
\ln k_{f1} = \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT_1}
\]
\[
\ln k_{f2} = \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT_2}
\]

Subtract the first equation from the second to eliminate \( \ln A \):

\[
\ln k_{f2} - \ln k_{f1} = \left( \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT_2} \right) - \left( \ln A - \frac{E_a}{RT_1} \right)
\]

\[
\ln \left( \frac{k_{f2}}{R_f1} \right) = \frac{E_a}{RT_1} - \frac{E_f2}{RT_2}
\]

\[
\ln \left( \frac{k_{f2}}{k_{f1}} \right) = \frac{E_a}{RT} \left( \frac{1}{T_1} - \frac{1}{T_2} \right)
\]

Solve for \( E_a \):

\[
E_a = \frac{R \ln \left( \frac{k_{f2}}{k_{f1}} \right)}{\frac{1}{T_1} - \frac{1}{T_2}}
\]

