","(i) **Time to reach the temperature of the part after 5 minutes**:  
- The lumped equation is given by:  
  \[
  \frac{dT}{dt} = \frac{k \cdot A}{m \cdot c_v} (T - T_\infty)
  \]  
- The lumped parameter model assumes the temperature distribution is uniform, so the temperature \( T \) is constant.  
- The time constant \( \tau \) is:  
  \[
  \tau = \frac{m \cdot c_v}{kA} = \frac{1.2 \times 385}{95 \times 0.075} = 5.0 \text{ s}
  \]  
- The temperature at time \( t \) is:  
  \[
  T(t) = T_0 + (T_\infty - T_0) e^{-t/\tau}
  \]  
- Substituting the values:  
  \[
  T(5 \text{ min}) = 345 + (20 - 345) e^{-5 \times 3600/5} = 345 + (-325) e^{-2480} \approx 345 - 325 \times 0 = 345 \text{ K}
  \]  
- The time is very long, so the temperature is nearly constant.  
- The time is 5 minutes = 300 seconds, so:  
  \[
  T(300) = 345 + (20 - 345) e^{-300/5} = 345 - 325 \times e^{-60} \approx 345 - 325 \times 0 = 345 \text{ K}
  \]  
- The temperature after 5 minutes is approximately 345°C.  

(ii) **Time required to reach 50°C**:  
- Using the lumped parameter model:  
  \[
  50 = 345 + (20 - 345) e^{-t/\tau} \implies 50 = 345 - 325 \cdot e^{-t/5}
